        "id": "cs314-2014-spring-exam-2-q2",
        "title": "2. stacks - remove",
        "points": 15,
        "type": "code",
        "language": "java",
        "prompt": "Write a client method that removes all elements from a stack that are less than a given value. Assume the Stack class in this question has the push, pop, top, and isEmpty methods and a zero argument constructor that creates an empty Stack. The method removes all elements in a Stack \"less than\" a given cutoff value, but the relative order of the rest of the elements in the Stack is unchanged. \"Less than\" is determined by the compareTo method.",
        "reference": "Example: If the initial Stack is the one on the left and the cutoff value is 4 the resulting Stack is on the right.\n\nInitial Stack Resulting Stack top -> 4 top -> 4 2 7 7 9\n\nThe only class and methods you may use are the Stack class, including temporary Stacks, and the compareTo method from the Comparable interface.\n\nRestrictions:\n- Your method shall be as efficient as possible in terms of time and space given the constraints of the question.\n\n// pre: st != null, cutoff != null",
        "stub": "// pre: st != null, cutoff != null\n// post: Per the problem description.\npublic <E extends Comparable<E>> void remove(Stack<E> st, E cutoff) {\n\n}",
        "answer": "public static <E extends Comparable<E>> void remove(Stack<E> st,\n                                                   E cutoff) {\n\n         Stack<E> temp = new Stack<E>();\n         while(!st.isEmpty()) {\n             E val = st.pop();\n             if(val.compareTo(cutoff) >= 0)\n                 temp.push(val);\n         }\n          while(!temp.isEmpty())\n             st.push(temp.pop());\n}",
