        "id": "cs314-2016-spring-final-q4",
        "title": "4. Binary Trees - numNodesLessThanSumOfAncestors",
        "points": 15,
        "type": "code",
        "language": "java",
        "prompt": "Complete the numNodesLessThanSumOfAncestors accessor method",
        "reference": "for a binary tree of ints class. The binary tree class for this question stores ints, but it is not a binary\n\nsearch tree.\n\nThe method returns the number of nodes in the tree that contain a value that is less than the sum of the values in that node's ancestor nodes. Recall ancestor nodes are all the nodes in the path from the root down to a node. A node is not an ancestor of itself.\n\nRestrictions:\n- You may use the nested BNode class, but no other Java classes or methods. Not even arrays.\n\nConsider the following trees and the expected results. The nodes that meet the criteria are bolded.\n\nempty tree -> returns 0\n\n5 -> returns 0 -5 -> returns 1 (sum of ancestors is 0)\n\n5 -> returns 1 5 -> returns 1 / \\ / 13 4 2\n\n5 -> returns 0 5 -> returns 2 / \\ / \\ 12 5 -5 4\n\n5 -> returns 4 / \\ -5 < 5\n\n-5 15 -1 < 0 (5 + -5)\n\n/ \\ / \\ -6 < -2 (5 + -5 + -1 + -1) 3 -1 25 30 840 < 850 (5 + 15 + 30 + / \\ 100 + 200 + 500)\n\n-1 100\n\n/ /\n\n-6 200\n\n\\ 500 \\ 840\n\npublic class BinaryTree {\n     private BNode root; // root == null iff tree is empty\n\n        private static class BNode {\n             private int value;\n             private BNode left;\n             private BNode right;\n        }\n}\n\nComplete the following instance method for the BinaryTree class. You may not use any other methods from the BinaryTree class unless you implement them as part of your answer.\n\n// pre: none\n// post: Returns the number of nodes in this tree that contain a value that is less than the sum of the values in the node's ancestor nodes.",
        "stub": "// pre: none\n// post: Per the problem description.\npublic int numNodesLessThanSumOfAncestors() {\n\n}",
        "answer": "public int numNodesLessThanSumOfAncestors() {\n       return helper(root, 0);\n}\n\nprivate int helper(BNode current, int sumOfAncestors) {\n     int result = 0;\n     if (current != null) {\n           // check if current node's less than sum of ancestors\n           if (current.value < sumOfAncestors) {\n                result++;\n           }\n           int newSum = sumOfAncestors + current.value;\n           result += helper(current.left, newSum);\n           result += helper(current.right, newSum);\n     }\n     return result; // if current == null, result still 0\n}",
        "runnable": false,
        "rubric": [
          {
            "label": "create helper method and call it correctly with sum of 0",
            "points": 2
          },
          {
            "label": "base case when current is null",
            "points": 3
          }
        ],
        "sourceNote": "exampdfs/cs314/2016-spring/final-exam-spring-2016.pdf, question 4"
