        "id": "cs314-2017-spring-exam-2-q3",
        "title": "3. Stacks and Queues - stacksAreEqual",
        "points": 20,
        "type": "code",
        "language": "java",
        "prompt": "Write a method that accepts two stacks as parameters and returns true if the stacks have the same number of elements in the same order, false otherwise. This method is NOT part of the Stack class, so you do not have access to the private instance variables of the Stack class. You may create and use a single stack as an auxiliary data structure in your method.",
        "reference": "Consider the following examples:\n\ns1 top -> 4 s2 top -> 4 returns true 3 3\n\ns1 top -> 4 s2 top -> 4 returns false 3 3 1 2\n\ns1 top -> 4 s2 top -> 4 returns false 3 3\n\ns1 top -> s2 top -> returns true (both stacks empty)\n\ns1 top -> s2 top -> 4 returns false (s1 empty)\n\nRestrictions:\n- You may assume none of the elements in either stack equal null.\n- You may use these methods for the stack class.\n- Do not use recursion.\n\nStack314: isEmpty, push, pop, top\n\nYou may also use the equals method declared in the Object class. Do not use any other Java classes or methods.\n\nNote, each stack must be restored to its original state by the time the method completes.\n\nComplete the method on the next page.\n\n// pre: s1 != null, s2 != null, no elements in s1 or s2 equal null\n// post: per the problem description",
        "stub": "// pre: s1 != null, s2 != null, no elements in s1 or s2 equal null\n// post: per the problem description\npublic <E> boolean stacksAreEqual(Stack314<E> s1, Stack314<E> s2) {\n\n}",
        "answer": "public <E> boolean stacksAreEqual(Stack314<E> s1, Stack314<E> s2) {\n     Stack314<E> tempStack = new Stack314<>();\n     boolean equal = true;\n     while (!s1.isEmpty() && !s2.isEmpty() && equal) {\n          // OR !(s1.isEmpty() || s2.isEmpty()) && equal\n          equal = s1.top().equals(s2.top());\n          tempStack.push(s1.pop());\n          tempStack.push(s2.pop());\n     }\n\n        // make sure both stacks are empty\n        equal = equal && s1.isEmpty() && s2.isEmpty();\n\n        // Now put the stuff we took out back.\n        while (!tempStack.isEmpty()) {\n             s2.push(tempStack.pop());\n             s1.push(tempStack.pop());\n        }\n        return equal;\n}",
        "runnable": false,
