        "id": "cs314-2019-fall-final-q4",
        "title": "4. Binary Trees - removeOddLeaves",
        "points": 15,
        "type": "code",
        "language": "java",
        "prompt": "Implement an instance method for a binary tree class that removes any leaves from the tree that have an odd depth.",
        "reference": "public class BinaryTree {\n\n       private BNode root; // root == null if size == 0\n       private int size; // number of nodes in this tree\n\n       // nested BNode class\n       private static class BNode {\n            private int data;\n            // left and right child are null if no child on that side\n            private BNode left;\n            private BNode right;\n       }\n}\n\nConsider the tree t on the left. This is not a binary search tree. If we remove all leaf nodes that at are at at odd depth the resulting tree is shown on to the right.\n\nBEFORE AFTER\n\nThe method updates the size field for the BinaryTree class and returns the number of nodes removed by the method.\n\nRestrictions:\n- Do not create any new nodes or other data structures.\n- You may use the BNode class, but do not use any other methods or classes. This includes arrays.\n- You may NOT add any class or instance variables to the BinaryTree or BNode classes.\n\nPart of the question grade (2 points) will be based on the clarity and conciseness of your solution.\n\n// pre: none, post per the problem description.",
        "stub": "// pre: none, post per the problem description.\n// post: Per the problem description.\npublic int removeOddLeaves() {\n\n}",
        "answer": "public int removeOddLeaves() {\n    int oldSize = size;\n    root = help(root, 0);\n    return oldSize - size;\n}\n\nprivate BNode help(BNode n, int depth) {\n    if (n != null) {\n        // System.out.println(depth + \" \" + n.data);\n        if (depth % 2 == 1 && ((n.left == null && n.right == null))) {\n            n = null;\n            size--;\n        } else {\n            n.left = help(n.left, depth + 1);\n            n.right = help(n.right, depth + 1);\n        }\n    }\n    return n;\n}",
