        "points": 20,
        "type": "code",
        "language": "java",
        "prompt": "This question uses the same GenericList as question 2. Write an instance method for the GenericList class, maxFrequency. The method accepts 3 parameters: - Another GenericList. This reference shall not equal null. - A target value. This reference shall not equal null. - A starting index. This value shall be greater than or equal to 0. The method returns a reference to the list (calling object or explicit parameter) that contains the most occurrences of the target element starting at the given index in the list. If there is a tie for the most elements, return the list with the smaller size, unless neither list contains any elements equal to the target value starting at the starting index. In that case, return null.",
        "reference": "Examples of calls to maxFrequency(GenericList<E> other, E tgt, int start) and the expected result. In these examples this lists contain Strings.\n\nExamples:\n[].maxFrequency([A, BB, A, C], A, 0) -> returns reference to other\n[].maxFrequency([A, BB, A, C], A, 1) -> returns reference to other\n[].maxFrequency([A, BB, A, C], A, 2) -> returns reference to other\n[].maxFrequency([A, BB, A, C], A, 3) -> returns null\n[A, A].maxFrequency([A, BB, A, C], A, 0) -> returns reference to the\n\ncalling object\n\nExamples:\n[A, A].maxFrequency([A, BB, A, C], A, 1) -> returns reference to the\n\ncalling object\n\nExamples:\n[A, A].maxFrequency([A, BB, A, C], A, 2) -> returns reference to other\n[A, A].maxFrequency([A, BB, A, C], A, 3) -> returns null\n[A, A].maxFrequency([A, BB, A, C], A, 6) -> returns null\n[A, A, B, CC, AA].maxFrequency([A, BB, A, C], X, 0) -> returns null\n\nRestrictions:\n- You may not use any methods from the GenericList class unless you implement them yourself as a part of your solution.\n- Do not use any other Java classes or methods except the Object equals method.\n\n// pre: other != null, tgt != null, start >= 0\n// post: per the problem description",
        "stub": "// pre: other != null, tgt != null, start >= 0\n// post: per the problem description\npublic GenericList<E> maxFrequency(GenericList<E> other, E tgt, int start) {\n\n}",
        "answer": "public GenericList<E> maxFrequency(GenericList<E> other, E tgt,\n           int start) {\n      int countThis = count(start, tgt);\n      int countOther = other.count(start, tgt);\n      if (countThis > countOther) {\n           return this;\n      } else if (countThis < countOther) {\n           return other;\n      } else {\n           // tie\n           if (countThis == 0) {\n               return null;\n           } else if (size < other.size) {\n               return this;\n           } else {\n               return other;\n           }\n      }\n}\nprivate int count(int st, E tgt) {\n      int result = 0;\n      for (int i = st; i < size; i++) {\n           if (con[i].equals(tgt)) {\n                 result++;\n           }\n      }\n      return result;\n}",
